# The Network: Syncthing
#
# Expects DIRECT.
#
# Global discovery and relays, plus the gateway's own client by process name. Announcing through a proxy registers the exit address as the device's endpoint, which defeats direct peer connections the same way a proxied STUN answer would. Peers and relays are dialled by bare address, so the inline TCP 22000 and 22067 rules in the profile are what keeps the transfers themselves direct; this file only covers the lookups and the local process.

DOMAIN-SUFFIX,syncthing.net
PROCESS-NAME,syncthing
